                    {
                        "sense_id": "0c7e50b0-2631-3193-b772-a0714a1eca6d",
                        "entry_id": "7854740b-e51a-3fce-9039-7f09925cb54b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The quality of being callous; emotional hardheartedness or indifference."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "94e806f6-44e1-451d-a01e-ae614901a686",
                                "sense_id": "0c7e50b0-2631-3193-b772-a0714a1eca6d",
                                "text": "Fred was known for his callousness; local panhandlers had long since learned not to try their sob stories on him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9c59e9cd-3147-41be-9392-29a28cffec86",
                                "sense_id": "0c7e50b0-2631-3193-b772-a0714a1eca6d",
                                "text": "To have killed Laploshka was one thing; to have kept his beloved money would have argued a callousness of feeling of which I was not capable."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ec308a45-d474-3df9-9ae3-9ab30315fa70",
                        "entry_id": "7854740b-e51a-3fce-9039-7f09925cb54b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The quality of having calluses."
